.TH tine-export-live 1  "live " 
.SH NAME
tine\-export\-live \- Write the read\-only Tine app, with the static site as its fallback
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtine export live\fR [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-all\-pages\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-replace\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIGRAPH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write the read\-only Tine app, with the static site as its fallback
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<DIRECTORY>\fR [default: publish]
Graph\-relative output directory
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-pages\fR
Publish every page, ignoring `public:: true` selection for this run
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable diagnostic logging for the desktop app
.TP
\fB\-\-replace\fR
Retire an existing output into recovery and install the new export
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<PAGE>\fR
Page to open first. Defaults to configured home, Welcome to Tine, or the first page
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Name shown in the published app. Defaults to the graph directory name
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIGRAPH\fR>

